<page route="/components/visualization">
  <catalog-document title="Boards, dashboards, flows and charts" description="Board controls, dashboard layouts, VueFlow diagrams and ECharts analytics components." current="/components">
    <nav class="reference-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#ref-board">board</a><a href="#ref-board-column">board-column</a><a href="#ref-board-card">board-card</a><a href="#ref-dashboard-grid">dashboard-grid</a><a href="#ref-dashboard-item">dashboard-item</a><a href="#ref-flow-editor">flow-editor</a><a href="#ref-chart">chart</a></nav>
    <reference-entry name="board"
      :api='"id: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\nreadOnly: Boolean = false\ndisabled: Boolean = false"'
      :contract='"Root receives attributes/classes. Default children are board-column components with application-owned content. The application supplies card data, valid destinations, authorization and saves. IDs are local to this board; scroll keys and preservation keys are unique in the surrounding rendered view. Board and column scroll positions survive refreshed content."'
      :keyboard='"The named board region supports native scrolling. Cards expose a Move button for pointer/touch dragging or a keyboard destination dialog. Readonly retains content and hides movement; disabled retains content while disabling moves. Without scripts, projected columns, content and links remain readable."'
      :css='"--board-height (620px), --board-column-min-width (260px), --board-gap (16px), --board-column-bg, --board-card-bg and shared palette/focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<board id=\"review\" label=\"Review board\">\n  <board-column columnId=\"todo\" label=\"To do\" scrollKey=\"review-todo\">Your cards</board-column>\n</board>"'>
      <board id="reference-board" label="Reference board" readOnly><board-column columnId="todo" label="To do" scrollKey="reference-board-todo"><board-card cardId="proposal" label="Proposal"><p class="catalog-description">Application-owned proposal content.</p></board-card></board-column><board-column columnId="done" label="Done" scrollKey="reference-board-done"><p class="catalog-description">No items.</p></board-column></board>
      <a class="catalog-link" href="/boards">Working boards in both palettes</a>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="board-column"
      :api='"columnId: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\nsummary: String = \"\"\nscrollKey: String (required)"'
      :contract='"A named column inside board, with projected cards or application-owned empty/quick-add content. The application supplies any count or WIP summary. columnId identifies movement destinations; scrollKey preserves this column’s vertical scroll through surrounding updates."'
      :keyboard='"Projected card links and controls retain their native keyboard behavior. The shared Move dialog can reach permitted destinations outside the current viewport. Pointer/touch dragging scrolls near the board and column edges."'
      :css='"--board-column-bg, --board-column-min-width, --board-gap, shared typography, border, radius and focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<board-column columnId=\"review\" label=\"Review\" summary=\"3 items\" scrollKey=\"proposal-review\">\n  Your application-owned cards\n</board-column>"'>
      <board id="reference-board-column" label="Reference column" readOnly><board-column columnId="review" label="Review" summary="1 item" scrollKey="reference-column-review"><board-card cardId="review" label="Review item"><p class="catalog-description">The application supplies this content and summary.</p></board-card></board-column></board>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="board-card"
      :api='"cardId: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\ntargets: List<bosca.design.model.BoardMoveTarget> = emptyList()\nmovable: Boolean = false\ndisabled: Boolean = false\npreserveKey: String = \"\""'
      :contract='"Default children remain application-owned BML content. Targets use BoardMoveTarget(id,label) and must identify rendered columns in this board. Stable preserveKey retains the body, local input and pending request while the card changes columns or surrounding content refreshes; change it when replacing the projected body. boardmove supplies {cardId,columnId,waitUntil}; register the application save promise synchronously. Rejection retains the card/destination and emits boarderror {cardId,columnId,message}. The library does not write application data."'
      :keyboard='"Activate Move with Enter or Space, then use the shared destination select and Move item. Arrow keys, Home and End select a destination. Escape dismisses the dialog or cancels a pointer/touch drag. Pending saves prevent repeat submission. Readonly/disabled states preserve ordinary projected content."'
      :css='"--board-card-bg, --board-column-bg and shared typography, control, border, radius and focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<board-card :cardId=\"item.id\" :label=\"item.title\" movable :targets=\"allowedTargets\" :preserveKey=\"item.id\">\n  <a :href=\"item.href\">{ item.title }</a>\n</board-card>"'>
      <board id="reference-board-card" label="Reference card" readOnly><board-column columnId="todo" label="To do" scrollKey="reference-card-todo"><board-card cardId="notes" label="Projected notes"><field label="Example note"><input value="Application content stays here" /></field></board-card></board-column></board>
      <a class="catalog-link" href="/boards">Movement, rejection and retained notes</a>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="dashboard-grid"
      :api='"id: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\nname: String = \"layout\"\nvalue: List<bosca.design.model.DashboardLayoutItem> = emptyList()\ncolumns: Int = 12\ncellHeight: Int = 60\nstackBelow: Int = 480\nlockedIds: Set<String> = emptySet()\nreadOnly: Boolean = false\ndisabled: Boolean = false\nerror: String = \"\"\npreserveKey: String = \"\""'
      :contract='"Root receives attributes/classes. Default children are direct dashboard-item widgets. value is a List<DashboardLayoutItem>; item IDs match itemId. Widget data stays in the application. layoutchange supplies {layout,itemId,kind}. Unlocked collisions push widgets downward; locked destinations are rejected. Stable preserveKey retains projected widget DOM and local layout; change it when adding/removing widget content. Applications own widget data, creation and saving."'
      :keyboard='"Tab reaches Move and Resize controls. Arrow keys change one cell. Pointer handles drag/resize; Escape or pointer cancellation restores the previous layout. Readonly, disabled, pending and locked widgets cannot move. Narrow containers stack without changing coordinates. Native reset restores the latest supplied layout. Without scripts, widgets stack and the labelled JSON form field remains visible."'
      :css='"--dashboard-gap (16px), --dashboard-item-bg, --dashboard-item-padding (16px), --dashboard-chart-height (260px), shared palette, border, typography and focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<dashboard-grid id=\"overview\" label=\"Overview\" :value=\"layout\" preserveKey=\"overview\">\n  <dashboard-item itemId=\"notes\" label=\"Notes\">Your BML content</dashboard-item>\n</dashboard-grid>"'>
      <dashboard-grid id="reference-dashboard" label="Reference dashboard" :value="bosca.design.catalog.CatalogSamples.referenceNotes"><dashboard-item itemId="notes" label="Notes"><p class="catalog-description">Move and resize this widget with its handles.</p></dashboard-item></dashboard-grid>
      <a class="catalog-link" href="/dashboards">Working dashboards in both palettes</a>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="dashboard-item"
      :api='"itemId: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)"'
      :contract='"A direct child of dashboard-grid. itemId matches one layout item and is local to that grid. label names the widget and handles. Additional attributes/classes reach the section; default children remain ordinary BML content in a scrolling body."'
      :keyboard='"The parent grid enables compact native Move/Resize buttons with arrow-key controls. Widget content retains its normal keyboard behavior and focus through geometry changes. Locked or readonly widgets keep their content usable."'
      :css='"--dashboard-item-bg, --dashboard-item-padding, shared palette, control border, radius and focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<dashboard-item itemId=\"visits\" label=\"Visits\">\n  <chart id=\"visits-chart\" label=\"Daily visits\" :config=\"chartConfig\" />\n</dashboard-item>"'>
      <dashboard-grid id="reference-dashboard-item" label="Reference widget" :value="bosca.design.catalog.CatalogSamples.referenceContent" readOnly><dashboard-item itemId="content" label="Widget content"><p class="catalog-description">Your own forms, charts and actions belong here.</p></dashboard-item></dashboard-grid>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="flow-editor"
      :api='"id: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\nname: String = \"graph\"\nvalue: bosca.design.model.FlowGraph = bosca.design.model.FlowGraph()\nreadOnly: Boolean = false\ndisabled: Boolean = false\nerror: String = \"\"\npreserveKey: String = \"\""'
      :contract='"Root receives additional attributes/classes and default children below the outline. VueFlow edits a Kotlin FlowGraph with typed nodes and edges. Application values belong in data.payload; textarea carries the native form value. flowchange supplies {graph}; flowselect supplies {kind,id,data}. Cancel flowconnect ({connection}) synchronously to reject a proposed edge. The application owns persistence, node settings and domain validation."'
      :keyboard='"Native Fit/zoom buttons and an expandable node/connection list remain reachable by Tab. Select a node, then use canvas arrow keys to move it. Delete is explicit through Remove selected. Named From/To controls provide keyboard connections. Read-only retains navigation; disabled excludes the form field. Without scripts the labelled JSON field remains visible."'
      :css='"--flow-height, --flow-bg, --flow-node-bg, --flow-edge, --flow-handle, shared palette, borders, typography and focus tokens."'
      :snippet='"<flow-editor id=\"pipeline\" label=\"Pipeline graph\" name=\"graph\" :value=\"graph\" preserveKey=\"pipeline\" />"'>
      <flow-editor id="reference-flow" label="Reference graph" :value="bosca.design.catalog.CatalogFlow.initial" readOnly />
      <a class="catalog-link" href="/flows">Working examples in both palettes</a>
    </reference-entry>
    <reference-entry name="chart"
      :api='"id: String (required)\nlabel: String (required)\nconfig: bosca.design.model.ChartConfiguration (required)\nmaps: Map<String, kotlinx.serialization.json.JsonObject> = emptyMap()\nloading: Boolean = false\nerror: String = \"\"\npreserveKey: String = \"\""'
      :contract='"Root receives additional attributes/classes and default children below the table. config is a Kotlin ChartConfiguration wrapping a native ECharts option object. maps provides named GeoJSON FeatureCollections for native map/geo references. chartselect supplies {datasetIndex,index,label,value} for canvas clicks and keyboard table actions. The application owns queries, result mapping and drill-down."'
      :keyboard='"The canvas has a name and an expandable server-rendered table supplies the same values without scripts. Tab reaches View data and each point action. Loading and errors reserve the chart footprint. Reduced motion disables animation. Built-in chart types include bar, line, scatter, pie, radar, heatmap, funnel and gauge, plus bubble, doughnut and polar-area variants and geographic data maps. Map controls zoom/reset; focused map arrow keys pan, plus/minus zoom, and Home resets. Native roam settings govern navigation."'
      :css='"--chart-height, --chart-bg, --chart-fg, --chart-grid, --chart-series-1 through --chart-series-6, shared palette and --font-sans. Explicit series colors take priority."'
      :snippet='"<chart id=\"visits\" label=\"Daily visits\" :config=\"chartConfig\" preserveKey=\"visits\" />"'>
      <chart id="reference-chart" label="Reference visits" :config='bosca.design.catalog.CatalogChart.configuration("line")' />
      <a class="catalog-link" href="/charts">Working examples in both palettes</a>
    </reference-entry>
  </catalog-document>
</page>
